    "raw": "Phase change: 505.12 K, melting point of Sn; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 1.680$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 8.466 + 0.348 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.879 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=8.466\\times10^{-3}T+0.174\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.879\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.834$ \nFormation equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-505.12 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hf}^{\\circ} = 4.505 - 0.117 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 2.420 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 72.900 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = 4.505 + 0.117 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T + 2.420 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 36.450 T^{-1} - 20.524 \\times 10^{-3} T$ \n505.12-2000 K: $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ}=2.540-1.340\\times10^{-3}T-0.258\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+250.700T^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = 2.540 + 1.340 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.258 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 125.350 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 23.502 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Pedley (396). ",
